+in those same tests pass first: e.g. `test_forward_chain_derives_fact_visible_to_backward_query`
+gets past `assertIn("Path A C", str(result))` and fails only at the query. Of the nine
+passes, eight never reach a query result — four validator tests, two forward/selection
+tests, and two acceptance-game tests that check arithmetic and source structure rather
+than run inference — and the ninth,
+`test_default_logic_keeps_pln_or_semantics`, passes vacuously: it asserts `proofs == []`.
